          "heading": "Fiji concede 351 points across their last 11 international matches",
          "body": "Fiji have struggled for defensive consistency of late, conceding 351 points across their last 11 games to average 31.9 points shipped per match. In the same 11-match window, the Flying Fijians scored 314 points, yielding an average of 28.5 points per game. This run included their biggest victory of the period, a 63-10 home win over Canada in September 2025 during the knockout stage of the Pacific Nations Cup."
