        {
          "kicker": "Transfer news",
          "heading": "Exeter Chiefs director Rob Baxter discusses Josh Iosefa-Scott France move",
          "body": "The future of Exeter Chiefs prop Josh Iosefa-Scott remains a significant talking point, with the tight-head expected to depart for France when his current contract expires next summer. While reports have linked the 30-year-old with a move to Provence, director of rugby Rob Baxter confirmed that no official destination has been finalised. Baxter noted that while Exeter remains in negotiations, the player has attracted a \"very good offer in France\" that reflects his consistent form over the past two seasons."
