          "kicker": "Selection call",
          "heading": "Jane Clohessy earns first Ireland start following family rugby legacy",
          "body": "Jane Clohessy made her first start for the Ireland women's side in yesterday's match against Japan at Virgin Media Park. The 27-year-old, daughter of Munster and Ireland legend Peter Clohessy, featured in the second row for the fixture. Reflecting on her transition to the international stage, Clohessy noted, “The whistle goes and you’re straight into it. I feel awful sorry for the girls that are stuck in their own head, I don’t know how I’d cope with that. I’d say it’s the way I’m wired.”"
